==Vice Versa==
*Characters from The Battle Cats have made cameos or temporary appearances in many of [[PONOS Corporation|PONOS]]' other games. An example is ''Heads Off'', in which [[The Face]] is [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NGkRmS9W6Sc one of the larger playable characters] and makes a lower-pitched screaming sound compared to the other characters.
**A more subtle example was [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:Kagami-Jijii|Kagami-Jijii]]'s attack animation in ''[[Yuru-i GeGeGe no Kitarou: Youkai Dotabata Daisensou]]'', which looked strikingly similar to [[Dark Emperor Nyandam]]'s.
*The "Neko DJ" in the ''Roblox'' game Tower Defense Simulator is a clear homage to [[Moneko (Special Cat)|Moneko]], even wearing a badge with the basic [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Cat]]'s face on it. Edit: In the v1.29.0 update, the reference was removed.
*One of the loadouts in the [[mh:itemasylum:JGN|JGN]] mode of the ''Roblox'' game Item Asylum is the Filibuster, which has a "fili-orb" attack resembling Filibuster Obstructa's attack animation and plays a [https://youtu.be/QJ2V6NxA1Ew remix] of his theme.
*One of the [[wikia:mystic-mansion:Artifacts/Just Kill Me 3|Artifacts]] in the games ''[[wikia:mystic-mansion:Just Kill Me.|Just Kill Me.]]'' and ''[[wikia:mystic-mansion:Just Kill Me 3|Just Kill Me 3]]'' is a "[[Cat Food|Cat Can]]" with the description, "If you collect cat cans, you can summon in some kind of world. Demon God doesn't really like it," referring to [[Cat Capsule#Rare Cat Capsules|Rare Cat Capsules]].
*[[w:SiIvaGunner|SiIvaGunner]] has produced several "high quality rips" of [[music]] tracks from the game, a list of which can be found [https://www.siivagunner.wiki/wiki/Category:The_Battle_Cats here].
*In [https://www.reddit.com/r/battlecats/comments/tbis70/fluff_kirby_does_his_best_impression_of_a_cat/ one page] of the ''Kirby'' manga [https://wikirby.com/wiki/Kirby_Manga_Mania ''Kirby Manga Mania''], Kirby himself copied the form of a [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Cat]].
*In ''[[wikipedia:Rick and Morty: The Anime|Rick and Morty: The Anime]]''<nowiki>'</nowiki>s first episode, ''Girl Who Manipulates Time'', a [[wikia:rickandmorty:Gromflomite|Gromflomite]] says that they might miss a limited event in The Battle Cats if a reply takes too long.
*Among the names Cats can randomly have in ''[[Wikipedia:Mewgenics|Mewgenics]]'' are "Kasli" (referencing [[Kasli the Scourge (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasli the Scourge]]/[[Kasli the Bane (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasli the Bane]]) and "[[Mr. Puffington]]".

